From 1bb6a63c466b6b2b9e649c1bae801b3deefc85c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonas=20=C3=85dahl?= <jadahl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 29 Aug 2025 00:02:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] window/wayland: Keep and use window drag hen config is
 acked

When we're moving a maximized window using a window drag, it will after
a threshold snap out of its maximized state. When a unmaximize
configuration is pending, don't actually move the window, but amend the
stored position in the pending configuration according to the window
drag position calculations.

Also keep track of what drag caused what unmaximize request, so that
when the unmaximized surface configuration is acknowledged, an up to
date position derived from the window drag can be calculated. Keep a
reference to the drag, so that even if the drag ended a position can be
calculated from the last state of the drag.

Closes: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/4281
